## Future design

What the design will cover later; nothing in this section is current behaviour.
- The manager GUI is a Fearless program of the standard library: it sends its messages with `CapManager`, and reads what the manager tells it with an API of the standard library still to be designed.
- The Output keeps only the last part of what a running main or a compilation prints.
- Removing or changing a data project mounted on a DataRead type of a code project shows a confirmation dialog in the manager GUI, naming the code projects that get a broken mount.

## Implementation notes

- The manager GUI is a Java program of Controllers, in a JVM of its own. `ManagerGui.start` starts it with the paths of the 'manager folder' and of the base cache, and keeps its standard input open as its 'parent lifeline' (AttenuationDesign): the manager tells the manager GUI what it tells on that standard input, and the manager GUI ends when the manager ends.
- On macOS the manager GUI shows no Dock icon of its own (`apple.awt.UIElement`): the Dock icon is the one of the manager.
- A desk, such as GNOME, may refuse to bring the 'manager window' to the front, and tell the user in its own way, for example with a notification that Fearless Manager is ready.
